{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>He is Aharon and Moshe.</b> These are the ones mentioned above, whom Yocheved bore to Amram. <b>He is Aharon and Moshe.</b> There are places that put Aharon before Moshe, and places that put Moshe before Aharon — to tell you that they are equal, as one." "<b>Upon their hosts.</b> In their hosts — all their host by their tribes. The עַל is used where it means only in the place of a single letter [ב], as in ״וְעַל חַרְבְּךָ תִּחְיֶה״ (Genesis 27) — like בְּחַרְבְּךָ, ״עֲמַדְתֶּם עַל חַרְבְּכֶם״ (Ezekiel 33) — בְּחַרְבְּכֶם."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:50:54.292703744Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}